    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by Alexander's general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> I, the dynasty lost Asia at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ipsus">Ipsus</a> in 301 BCE but won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-ii-gonatas">Antigonus II Gonatas</a>.</li><li>From Pella its kings dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarissa">sarissa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> and garrisons at Corinth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrias">Demetrias</a>.</li><li>Philip V's alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> began a series of wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> that ended at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pydna">Pydna</a> in 168 BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colossus-of-rhodes">Colossus of Rhodes</a> is said to have been paid for by selling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-engine">siege engines</a> that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-i-of-macedon">Demetrius Poliorcetes</a> left behind after his failed siege of the city in 305–304 BCE.</p></aside>
    </section>

